# Finsler–Hadwiger theorem — two squares sharing a vertex: their centers and the midpoints of the two connecting segments form a square (here: equal diagonals) (source: Finsler & Hadwiger 1937)
A B = segment
C D = square(A, B)
E = free
F G = square(A, E)
O1 = midpoint(A, C)
O2 = midpoint(A, F)
M1 = midpoint(B, G)
M2 = midpoint(D, E)
prove cong(O1, O2, M1, M2)
